// Key findings:
// 1. semantics.simplify() returned _resolved dicts, not proper tree nodes
//    Fix: return bool/child node directly
// 2. inject_context was NOT propagated by _evaluate_operator
//    Fix: propagate flag from parent to children
// 3. vsf-rsi had record/match but no adapt/learn
//    Fix: implement adapt() + learn() in scenario_memory.py
// 4. rsi_socratic_bridge.py enables dynamic predicate registration
//    Pattern: @engine.register('name') + inject_context=True in tree
// 5. bash failures were NOT captured by RSI
//    Fix: expand plugin condition to include bash+failure

@insight "The gap between simplify() and evaluate() was a type mismatch — resolved dicts vs tree nodes. Always return the same type the consumer expects."
@insight "inject_context propagation is fundamental — without it, nested predicates can't evaluate. This should be a core engine feature, not a workaround."
@insight "adapt() + learn() close the learning loop — without them, RSI just records but never improves."

